---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { emailConsent, newsletter, site } from '../data/site';
const updated = 'November 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="What this website collects when you get a free resource or join the email list, why, and how to have it deleted.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <p>
        This website belongs to {site.name}. This page explains what is collected when you get a free resource or join the email list, who
        else handles it, and how you can have it deleted.{' '}
        {site.email ? <>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</> : <>Questions: reply to any email you have received from me.</>}
      </p>

      <h2>When you get a free resource</h2>
      <p>Free prompts, templates, guides and files on this site are unlocked with your name and email address. I store:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name and email address;</li>
        <li>which resource you asked for, the page you were on, and the date and time;</li>
        <li>your IP address, the country it points to, and your browser type, as a record of where the request came from;</li>
        <li>the exact wording you agreed to under the form;</li>
        <li>which resources you open and which files you download afterwards.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The wording you agree to is:</p>
      <blockquote>{emailConsent.text}</blockquote>

      <h2>Who else handles your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Hostinger</b> hosts the website and the database where the list is stored.</li>
        <li><b>Resend</b> delivers the emails I send you.</li>
        <li><b>Kit</b> runs {newsletter.name}; your address is also added to that list when you sign up here.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Unsubscribing and deleting your data</h2>
      <p>
        Every email has a one-click unsubscribe link. After you unsubscribe I stop emailing you, and the resources you unlocked keep working.
        To have your record deleted completely, ask by replying to one of my emails from the address you signed up with.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        A small cookie remembers that you already unlocked a resource, so you are not asked again on the same browser. Nothing is used for
        advertising.
      </p>

      <p>If this policy changes, the new version appears on this page with a new date.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
